  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord may require a tenant to pay a rent deposit with respect to a tenancy if the landlord does so on or before entering into the tenancy agreement.",
  "reason": "Section 106 of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 permits a landlord to require a rent deposit upon entering into a tenancy agreement, provided it does not exceed the rent for one rental period (one month here) and is applied solely to the rent for the last period before the tenancy terminates."
}

